        <!-- ============ Page 8: FERS Survivor Benefit Annuity (FERS only) ============ -->
        <apex:outputPanel layout="none" rendered="{!Lead.FERS__c == true}">
        <table class="gfgp-sheet">
            <tr>
                <td class="gfgp-body">
                    <!-- Section A: FERS - Calculating FERS Retirement (continued) -->
                    <div class="gfgp-title">FERS - Calculating FERS Retirement</div>
                    <div class="gfgp-accent"></div>

                    <table class="gfgp-cmp">
                        <colgroup><col style="width:22%" /><col style="width:26%" /><col style="width:26%" /><col style="width:26%" /></colgroup>
                        <!-- Scenario 1 -->
                        <tr>
                            <td class="l"><span class="vblank"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0}"><apex:param value="{!fcS1RetirementAge}" /></apex:outputText></span></td>
                            <td><span class="vblank"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsS1CurrentMonthlyIncome}" /></apex:outputText></span></td>
                            <td><span class="vblank"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsS1MonthlyRetirementAnnuity}" /></apex:outputText></span></td>
                            <td><span class="vblank"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsS1DifferenceInMonthlyAnnuity}" /></apex:outputText></span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="hd">
                            <td class="l">Age at Retirement</td>
                            <td>Current Monthly Income</td>
                            <td>Monthly Retirement Annuity</td>
                            <td>Difference in Monthly Annuity</td>
                        </tr>
                        <!-- Scenario 2 -->
                        <tr>
                            <td class="l"><span class="vblank"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0}"><apex:param value="{!fcS2RetirementAge}" /></apex:outputText></span></td>
                            <td><span class="vblank"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsS2CurrentMonthlyIncome}" /></apex:outputText></span></td>
                            <td><span class="vblank"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsS2MonthlyRetirementAnnuity}" /></apex:outputText></span></td>
                            <td><span class="vblank"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsS2DifferenceInMonthlyAnnuity}" /></apex:outputText></span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="hd">
                            <td class="l">Age at Retirement</td>
                            <td>Current Monthly Income</td>
                            <td>Monthly Retirement Annuity</td>
                            <td>Difference in Monthly Annuity</td>
                        </tr>
                    </table>

                    <!-- Section B: FERS - Survivor Benefit Annuity (married / registered partnership) -->
                    <apex:outputPanel layout="none"
                        rendered="{!Lead.Marital_Status__c == 'Married' || Lead.Marital_Status__c == 'Registered Partnership'}">
                    <div class="gfgp-title">FERS - Survivor Benefit Annuity</div>
                    <div class="gfgp-accent"></div>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">Retiring federal employees under both the CSRS and FERS retirement systems have the opportunity to ensure continuation of benefits to survivors with an insurable interest. A person with an insurable interest is an insurance term applying to a person who would benefit financially by your continuation of life. Such persons would include, but are not limited to, a widow, widower, former spouse, and children.</p>
                    <ul class="gfgp-red-ul">
                        <li>May elect a survivor benefit of either 25% or 50% of their retirement annuity</li>
                        <li>If 25% is elected, their annuity will be reduced by 5%</li>
                        <li>If 50% is elected, their annuity will be reduced by 10%</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">To provide a survivor annuity for a person who has an "insurable interest" in you, your annual annuity would be reduced from 10 to 40 percent, depending on the difference in your age and the age of the person named.</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">Age of the person named in relation to the retiring employee and the corresponding reduction in annuity:</p>

                    <table style="width:100%;"><tr>
                        <td style="width:58%;vertical-align:top;">
                            <ul class="gfgp-ul">
                                <li>Older, same age, or less than 5 years younger 10% =</li>
                                <li>5 but less than 10 years younger 15% =</li>
                                <li>10 but less than 15 years younger 20% =</li>
                                <li>15 but less than 20 years younger 25% =</li>
                                <li>20 but less than 25 years younger 30% =</li>
                                <li>25 but less than 30 years younger 35% =</li>
                                <li>30 or more years younger 40%</li>
                            </ul>
                        </td>
                        <td style="width:42%;vertical-align:top;padding-left:10px;">
                            <div class="gfgp-callout">
                                <div class="gfgp-callout-title">Points to Consider</div>
                                If you opt out of the survivor benefit, your spouse or any other family member covered under FEHB will lose that coverage if you predecease them during retirement, unless they are otherwise eligible for coverage. In addition, they will lose the ability to initially enroll in FLTCIP coverage, unless otherwise eligible, although they could continue coverage if already enrolled.
                            </div>
                        </td>
                    </tr></table>

                    <!-- Minimum / Maximum Survivor Benefit boxes -->
                    <table style="width:100%;margin-top:12pt;"><tr>
                        <td style="width:50%;vertical-align:top;padding-right:14px;">
                            <div class="gfgp-survbox">
                                <div class="gfgp-survbox__title">Minimum Survivor Benefit Monthly Cost</div>
                                <table class="gfgp-calc">
                                    <tr><td>Monthly Annuity: $</td><td class="v"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsMonthlyAnnuity}" /></apex:outputText></td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Minus 5%</td><td class="v"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsMinus5Pct}" /></apex:outputText></td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Reduced Annuity: $</td><td class="v"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsReducedMin}" /></apex:outputText></td></tr>
                                </table>
                                <div class="gfgp-survcap">25% Reduction<br/>Surviving Spouse Monthly Income<br/>$ <span class="u"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsSurvivingSpouseMin}" /></apex:outputText></span></div>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                        <td style="width:50%;vertical-align:top;">
                            <div class="gfgp-survbox">
                                <div class="gfgp-survbox__title">Maximum Survivor Benefit Monthly Cost</div>
                                <table class="gfgp-calc">
                                    <tr><td>Monthly Annuity: $</td><td class="v"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsMonthlyAnnuity}" /></apex:outputText></td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Minus 10%</td><td class="v"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsMinus10Pct}" /></apex:outputText></td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Reduced Annuity: $</td><td class="v"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsReducedMax}" /></apex:outputText></td></tr>
                                </table>
                                <div class="gfgp-survcap">50% Reduction<br/>Surviving Spouse Monthly Income<br/>$ <span class="u"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!fsSurvivingSpouseMax}" /></apex:outputText></span></div>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                    </tr></table>
                    </apex:outputPanel>
                </td>
                <td class="gfgp-rail" valign="bottom"><div class="gfgp-pageno">8</div></td>
            </tr>
        </table>
        </apex:outputPanel>

        <!-- ============ Page 9: FERS Special Groups (Special Group only) ============ -->
        <apex:outputPanel layout="none" rendered="{!Lead.Special_Group_Member__c == true}">
        <table class="gfgp-sheet">
            <tr>
                <td class="gfgp-rail" valign="bottom"><div class="gfgp-pageno">9</div></td>
                <td class="gfgp-body">
                    <div class="gfgp-title">FERS - Special Groups</div>
                    <div class="gfgp-accent"></div>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">Members of special groups, such as <u>law enforcement officers, firefighters and air traffic controllers</u>, pay different levels of employee contributions toward retirement and are eligible for retirement under age and service combinations that differ from those that apply for the standard retirement.</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">Law enforcement officers and firefighters under the FERS system are defined to be classified as special group employees if the position held is limited to "young and vigorous" personnel. In addition, they must have occupied a primary, first-line law enforcement, or firefighter position for at least 3 years before moving to a secondary (administrative or supervisory) position.</p>

                    <!-- Two-column block: bullets (left) + formula example (right) -->
                    <table style="width:100%;margin-top:8pt;"><tr>
                        <td style="width:48%;vertical-align:top;padding-right:12px;">
                            <p class="gfgp-center" style="font-weight:bold;margin:0 0 4pt;">FERS Special Groups</p>
                            <ul class="gfgp-ul">
                                <li>You can retire with unreduced benefits at age 50, with at least 20 years of creditable service</li>
                                <li>At any age, with at least 25 years of creditable service</li>
                                <li class="gfgp-li-red">Age 50 with at least 20 years of service (unreduced benefit)</li>
                                <li class="gfgp-li-red">Any age, with at least 25 years of creditable service (unreduced benefit)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </td>
                        <td style="width:52%;vertical-align:top;">
                            <p class="gfgp-eg" style="color:#B91C1C;font-weight:bold;">The formula for Special Groups is:</p>
                            <p class="gfgp-eg">1.7% X high-three X (first) 20 years and 1% X high-three for any amount over 20 years</p>
                            <p class="gfgp-eg">Example: A 53 year old with 23 years of service and a high-three of $115,000</p>
                            <p class="gfgp-eg">1.7% X <b><u>$115,000</u></b> = <b><u>$1,955.00</u></b> X (first) 20 years of service = <b><u>$39,100</u></b></p>
                            <p class="gfgp-eg">1% X <b><u>$115,000</u></b> high-three = <b><u>$1,150.00</u></b> X (remaining) three years = <b><u>$3,450</u></b></p>
                            <p class="gfgp-eg-total">Total FERS Annuity ($39,100+$3,450) = $42,550.00 Annually</p>
                        </td>
                    </tr></table>

                    <!-- Live calculation (this lead) -->
                    <div class="gfgp-calc-section">
                        <table class="gfgp-fcalc">
                            <tr>
                                <td>1.7% X</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.High_3_Salary__c}" /></apex:outputText><span class="sub">High-Three</span></td>
                                <td>=</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!sgFactor17xHigh3}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                                <td>X 20 Years =</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!sgBlock20YearAnnuity}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                            </tr>
                        </table>
                        <table class="gfgp-fcalc">
                            <tr>
                                <td>1% X</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.High_3_Salary__c}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                                <td>=</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!sgFactor01xHigh3}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                                <td>X</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0.##}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.Remaining_Years__c}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                                <td>Years =</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!sgFactor01xRemainingAnnuity}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                            </tr>
                        </table>
                        <table class="gfgp-fcalc">
                            <tr>
                                <td>Total Annual Annuity:</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!sgTotalAnnual}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                                <td>&#247; 12 =</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!sgTotalMonthly}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                                <td>Monthly</td>
                            </tr>
                        </table>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Air Traffic Controllers -->
                    <div class="gfgp-center-h" style="margin-top:14pt;">Air Traffic Controllers</div>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">Special Provisions: Vision 100 - Century Reauthorization Act was adopted February 10, 2004 and will impact the mandatory retirement calculation under CSRS and FERS.</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-p" style="font-weight:bold;margin-bottom:0;">Highlights:</p>
                    <ul class="gfgp-ul">
                        <li>Second-level supervisor will not be subject to mandatory retirement</li>
                        <li>Applies to active ATC with a date of birth prior to January 1, 1965</li>
                        <li>Retires on MRA (MRA is between 55 and 57, depending on date of birth)</li>
                        <li>With 30 years of service</li>
                        <li>At least 5 years of service as an ATC</li>
                        <li>Second-level supervisors under FERS will make additional deposits</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="gfgp-center-h">Calculating FERS Annuity Under Vision 100</div>
                    <p class="gfgp-center">1.7% for all years of service (even those over 20 years) except military buyback</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-center">Military buy back years will be calculated at 1%</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-center">If a FERS ATC at 1.7% COLA will not start until age 62</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
        </table>
        </apex:outputPanel>

        <!-- ============ Page 10: FERS Special Supplement (gated) ============ -->
        <apex:outputPanel layout="none" rendered="{!ssShowSpecialSupp}">
        <table class="gfgp-sheet">
            <tr>
                <td class="gfgp-body">
                    <div class="gfgp-title">FERS - Special Supplement</div>
                    <div class="gfgp-accent"></div>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">Also known as the Special Retirement Supplement or SRS. It is designed to help bridge the income gap for certain FERS employees who retire before age 62. It will supplement your missing Social Security income until you reach age 62 and then stop. Since the SRS is not paid by Social Security, you do not have to start receiving benefits from Social Security at age 62. You may delay taking these benefits to help increase your future Social Security annuity.</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">To be eligible, you must have a normal immediate retirement, not an early retirement (MRA+10). <span style="color:#B91C1C;">This means you must have 30 years of creditable service and meet your MRA, or you can have 20 years of creditable service and be age 60.</span></p>

                    <p class="gfgp-center">To recap, you may be eligible if:</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-center">You retire voluntarily | On an Immediate Annuity | Annuity not reduced for age</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-center">You may still be eligible if you:</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-center">Retire involuntarily before attaining MRA | Because of a major reorganization | Reduction in force</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-center">You are <i>not</i> eligible if:</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-center">You receive a deferred annuity benefit | Disability benefit | Immediate MRA + 10 annuity benefit</p>

                    <hr class="gfgp-rule" />

                    <p class="gfgp-center" style="color:#B91C1C;font-weight:bold;">Eligibility</p>
                    <ul class="gfgp-ul">
                        <li>You must be a FERS employee</li>
                        <li>You must retire on a full immediate retirement</li>
                        <li>Have 25 years of creditable service under Special Provisions and be any age or have 20 years of creditable service under Special Provisions and be at least 50 years old.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="gfgp-p" style="color:#B91C1C;">Note: If you do not have enough years of creditable service under Special Provisions, you may qualify for the FERS Supplement, if you retire under the regular FERS immediate retirement rules, see above.</p>

                    <hr class="gfgp-rule" />

                    <div class="gfgp-center-h">How the Earnings Test affects your SRS</div>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">Although the SRS is not paid by Social Security, it is subject to the Earnings Test. This is the amount of income allowed before Social Security benefits would be affected. This also applies to the SRS. For 2026, the exempt amount you can earn before Social Security benefit withholdings is $24,480 annually or $2,040 monthly if you are under full retirement age for the entire year. After reaching the exempt amount, benefits are reduced by $1.00 for every $2.00 earned over the limit.</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">For current exempt amounts please visit: <a class="gfgp-link" href="https://www.ssa.gov/OACT/COLA/rtea.html">https://www.ssa.gov/OACT/COLA/rtea.html</a></p>

                    <hr class="gfgp-rule" />

                    <p class="gfgp-p">Example: your SRS is $1470 monthly and you earned an additional $2110 that month.</p>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">$2110 (earned) - $2040 (exempt amount) = $70 over exempt amount divided by 2 = $35 Deducted from SRS payment.</p>
                    <ul class="gfgp-ul">
                        <li>The Earnings Test does not apply to Special Groups until they reach their regular FERS Minimum Retirement Age (MRA) at which point the Earnings Test will apply</li>
                        <li>It is possible that your SRS could reduce to $0.00</li>
                        <li>If you receive the SRS, you must report your earnings to OPM</li>
                    </ul>

                    <!-- FERS Special Supplement calculation -->
                    <div class="gfgp-calc-section">
                        <div class="gfgp-center-h" style="letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;">FERS Special Supplement</div>
                        <table class="gfgp-fcalc">
                            <tr>
                                <td>Years of Service:</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0.##}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.YOS_Special_Supplement__c}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                                <td>&#247; 40 =</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0.0}"><apex:param value="{!ssSupplementPct}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                                <td>%</td>
                            </tr>
                        </table>
                        <table class="gfgp-fcalc">
                            <tr>
                                <td>Social Security @ 62</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.Predicted_Social_Security__c}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                                <td>X</td>
                                <td class="b"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0.0}"><apex:param value="{!ssSupplementPct}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                                <td>% =</td>
                                <td class="b" style="color:#B91C1C;border-bottom-color:#B91C1C;"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!ssSupplementDollars}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                            </tr>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </td>
                <td class="gfgp-rail" valign="bottom"><div class="gfgp-pageno">10</div></td>
            </tr>
        </table>
        </apex:outputPanel>

        <!-- ============ Page 11: TSP, Resources, Forms ============ -->
        <table class="gfgp-sheet">
            <tr>
                <td class="gfgp-rail" valign="bottom"><div class="gfgp-pageno">11</div></td>
                <td class="gfgp-body">
                    <!-- Section A: TSP -->
                    <div class="gfgp-title">TSP - Thrift Savings Plan</div>
                    <div class="gfgp-accent"></div>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">The Thrift Savings Plan (TSP) is a retirement savings and investment plan for Federal employees and members of the uniformed services, including the Ready Reserve. It was established by Congress in the Federal Employees' Retirement System Act of 1986. For FERS employees, TSP is one of a three-part retirement package that also includes your FERS basic annuity and Social Security. For a FERS employee to take full advantage of this plan, they should contribute 5% to receive the full matching benefit. CSRS employees receive no matching funds.</p>

                    <table style="width:100%;margin-top:6pt;">
                        <colgroup><col style="width:46%" /><col style="width:20%" /><col style="width:34%" /></colgroup>
                        <tr>
                            <!-- Column 1: Contribution Limits + Current -->
                            <td style="vertical-align:top;padding-right:10px;">
                                <table class="gfgp-contrib">
                                    <tr><td class="gfgp-uhead">Contribution Limits</td><td class="gfgp-uhead" style="text-align:center;">Current</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>&#8226; Regular Contribution</td><td class="val"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $###,###}"><apex:param value="{!tspRegularLimit}" /></apex:outputText></td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>&#8226; Catch-Up Contribution<span class="sub"><br/>for employees over age 50</span></td><td class="val"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $###,###}"><apex:param value="{!tspCatchUpLimit}" /></apex:outputText></td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>&#8226; Total Contribution</td><td class="val"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $###,###}"><apex:param value="{!tspTotalContribution}" /></apex:outputText></td></tr>
                                </table>
                                <p class="gfgp-tspnote">Visit <a class="gfgp-link" href="https://www.tsp.gov/making-contributions/contribution-limits/">https://www.tsp.gov/making-contributions/contribution-limits/</a> or scan the QR code for <u>current</u> Contribution Limits</p>
                            </td>
                            <!-- Column 2: QR code -->
                            <td style="vertical-align:top;text-align:center;">
                                <apex:image url="{!$Resource.Pg12GrovesQR}" width="100" height="100" alt="Current Contribution Limits QR" />
                            </td>
                            <!-- Column 3: Government Matching -->
                            <td style="vertical-align:top;padding-left:10px;">
                                <p class="gfgp-uhead">Government Matching Contributions</p>
                                <ul class="gfgp-ul">
                                    <li>CSRS and CSRS Offset employees receive no matching funds</li>
                                    <li>FERS employees receive up to 5% of personal contributions
                                        <ul class="gfgp-circ">
                                            <li>1% agency automatic contribution</li>
                                            <li>1%-3% of employee contributions are matched at 100%</li>
                                            <li>4%-5% of employee contributions are matched at 50%</li>
                                        </ul>
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    </table>

                    <!-- TSP Options in Retirement -->
                    <div class="gfgp-center" style="margin-top:8pt;">
                        <div class="gfgp-options-heading" style="color:#B91C1C;font-weight:bold;text-decoration:underline;font-size:11pt;margin-bottom:4pt;">TSP Options in Retirement</div>
                        <table style="margin:0 auto;border-collapse:collapse;">
                            <tr><td class="gfgp-tspopt" style="text-align:left;">Monthly Payments</td><td class="gfgp-tspopt" style="text-align:left;">Rollover</td></tr>
                            <tr><td class="gfgp-tspopt" style="text-align:left;">Annuitize</td><td class="gfgp-tspopt" style="text-align:left;">Do Nothing</td></tr>
                        </table>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Section B: Resources -->
                    <div class="gfgp-title" style="margin-top:16pt;">Resources</div>
                    <div class="gfgp-accent"></div>
                    <p class="gfgp-p">Information in this workbook came from many sources (see below) and, due to time and space, has been condensed to offer you a basic overview. It is not meant to provide a detailed explanation of all benefits. Below are links with extensive information on the benefits which we covered during our review. Should you have additional questions, please review these links and contact us so we may assist you further.</p>
                    <div class="gfgp-linkrow">Federal Retirement: <a class="gfgp-link" href="http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/publications-forms/pamphlets/ri90-8.pdf">http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/publications-forms/pamphlets/ri90-8.pdf</a></div>
                    <div class="gfgp-linkrow">FERS: <a class="gfgp-link" href="http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/fers-information/">http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/fers-information/</a></div>
                    <div class="gfgp-linkrow">CSRS: <a class="gfgp-link" href="http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/csrs-information/">http://www.opm.gov/retirement-services/csrs-information/</a></div>
                    <div class="gfgp-linkrow">FEGLI: <a class="gfgp-link" href="http://www.opm.gov/healthcare-insurance/life-insurance/">http://www.opm.gov/healthcare-insurance/life-insurance/</a></div>
                    <div class="gfgp-linkrow">TSP: <a class="gfgp-link" href="https://www.tsp.gov/index.html">https://www.tsp.gov/index.html</a></div>
                    <div class="gfgp-linkrow">Social Security: <a class="gfgp-link" href="https://www.ssa.gov/">https://www.ssa.gov/</a></div>
                    <div class="gfgp-linkrow">Windfall Elimination Provision (WEP): <a class="gfgp-link" href="http://www.socialsecurity.gov/pubs/EN-05-10045.pdf">http://www.socialsecurity.gov/pubs/EN-05-10045.pdf</a></div>
                    <div class="gfgp-linkrow">Government Pension Offset (GPO): <a class="gfgp-link" href="http://www.socialsecurity.gov/pubs/EN-05-10007.pdf">http://www.socialsecurity.gov/pubs/EN-05-10007.pdf</a></div>

                    <!-- Section C: Forms For Collecting Benefits -->
                    <div class="gfgp-title" style="margin-top:16pt;">Forms For Collecting Benefits</div>
                    <div class="gfgp-accent"></div>
                    <table class="gfgp-mtr">
                        <tr><td class="hdr" colspan="2">MILITARY TIME RECAPTURE</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="branch">Army</td><td>DFAS - Indianapolis Center, ATTN: IN-FO-FC-A, 8899 E 56, Indianapolis, IN 46249-0875. Fax: 317-542-2779</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="branch">Navy</td><td>Director, DFAS - Cleveland Center-JJCS/FMCS, Anthony J. Celebreeze Federal Bldg., Cleveland, OH 44199-2055. Fax: 216-522-5974</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="branch">Air Force</td><td>DFAS-DE/FUPBC, 6760 East Irvington Place, Denver CO 80279-5000. Fax: 303-676-7408</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="branch">Marines</td><td>DFAS - Kansas City Center, 1500 East 95th Street, Kansas City, MO 64197-0001. Fax: 800-929-4207</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="branch">Coast Guard</td><td>Commanding Officer Settlements and Records, U.S. Coast Guard, Military Pay and Personnel Center, 444 SE Quincy Street, Topeka, KS 66683-3591</td></tr>
                    </table>
                </td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <!-- ============ Page 12: Financial Snapshot ============ -->
        <table class="gfgp-sheet">
            <tr>
                <td class="gfgp-body">
                    <div class="gfgp-title">Financial Snapshot</div>
                    <div class="gfgp-accent"></div>

                    <!-- Top row: logo (left) + date (right) -->
                    <table style="width:100%;margin-bottom:8pt;">
                        <tr>
                            <td style="vertical-align:middle;"><apex:image url="{!$Resource.Pg13GrovesLogo}" width="200" alt="Groves Financial Group" /></td>
                            <td style="vertical-align:middle;text-align:right;font-size:10.5pt;">Date: <span style="display:inline-block;min-width:80pt;border-bottom:1px solid #2b2b2b;text-align:center;"><apex:outputText value="{0, date, MM/dd/yyyy}"><apex:param value="{!TODAY()}" /></apex:outputText></span></td>
                        </tr>
                    </table>

                    <!-- Employee + Spouse name -->
                    <table class="gfgp-snap" style="margin-bottom:4pt;">
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Employee Name:</td>
                            <td class="uval" style="width:28%;"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.Name}" /></td>
                            <td class="extra">Spouse Name: <span class="u"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.Spouse_Name__r.Name}" /></span></td>
                        </tr>
                    </table>

                    <!-- Current Age / Age at Retirement -->
                    <table class="gfgp-snap" style="margin-bottom:6pt;">
                        <tr>
                            <td style="width:50%;">Current Age:
                                <span style="display:inline-block;min-width:36pt;border-bottom:1px solid #2b2b2b;text-align:center;"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.Contact_Age__c}" /></apex:outputText></span>
                            </td>
                            <td style="width:50%;">Age at Retirement:
                                <span style="display:inline-block;min-width:36pt;border-bottom:1px solid #2b2b2b;text-align:center;">
                                    <apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0}" rendered="{!Lead.Scenario1_Primary__c == true}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.Scenario1_Retirement_Age__c}" /></apex:outputText>
                                    <apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0}" rendered="{!Lead.Scenario2_Primary__c == true}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.Scenario2_Retirement_Age__c}" /></apex:outputText>
                                    <apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0}" rendered="{!AND(Lead.Scenario1_Primary__c == false, Lead.Scenario2_Primary__c == false)}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.Expected_Retirement_Age__c}" /></apex:outputText>
                                </span>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    </table>

                    <!-- Section A: Monthly Expenses -->
                    <div class="gfgp-seclabel">Monthly Expenses</div>
                    <table class="gfgp-snap">
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Pension:</td>
                            <td class="sign">&#160;</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!snapPensionBase}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                            <td class="extra">
                                <apex:outputPanel layout="none" rendered="{!snapIsMarried}">Surviving Spouse Benefit:
                                    <span class="u">
                                        <apex:outputText value="$0.00" rendered="{!snapSpouseBenefitOptedOut}" />
                                        <apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}" rendered="{!NOT(snapSpouseBenefitOptedOut)}"><apex:param value="{!snapSurvivingSpouseBenefit}" /></apex:outputText>
                                    </span><apex:outputText value=" OPTED OUT" styleClass="opt" rendered="{!snapSpouseBenefitOptedOut}" />
                                </apex:outputPanel>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Taxes: 12% 15% 20% 25%</td>
                            <td class="sign">-</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.taxRate3_Picklist__c}" /></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Health:</td>
                            <td class="sign">-</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.Total_Health__c}" /></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Additional Insurance:</td>
                            <td class="sign">-</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.Additional_Insurance__c}" /></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="tot">
                            <td class="lab">Total:</td>
                            <td class="sign">=</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!snapExpenseTotal}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                    </table>

                    <!-- Section B: Retirement Income -->
                    <div class="gfgp-seclabel">Retirement Income</div>
                    <table class="gfgp-snap">
                        <apex:outputPanel layout="none" rendered="{!snapYosFormulaVisible}">
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Formula Years of Service:</td>
                            <td class="sign">&#160;</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.YOS_Special_Supplement__c}" /></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#247; 40 = <span class="u"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0.0}"><apex:param value="{!snapYosPercent}" /></apex:outputText>%</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        </apex:outputPanel>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">FERS Special Supplement:</td>
                            <td class="sign">+</td>
                            <td class="uval">
                                <apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}" rendered="{!snapFersSupplementEligible}"><apex:param value="{!snapFersSupplementDisplay}" /></apex:outputText>
                                <apex:outputText value="Not Eligible" styleClass="ne" rendered="{!NOT(snapFersSupplementEligible)}" />
                            </td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Social Security:</td>
                            <td class="sign">+</td>
                            <td class="uval">
                                <apex:outputField value="{!Lead.Predicted_Social_Security__c}" rendered="{!snapSocialSecurityEligible}" />
                                <apex:outputText value="Not Eligible" styleClass="ne" rendered="{!NOT(snapSocialSecurityEligible)}" />
                            </td>
                            <td class="extra">Start Age:
                                <span class="u">
                                    <apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0}" rendered="{!Lead.Scenario1_Primary__c == true}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.Scenario1_Retirement_Age__c}" /></apex:outputText>
                                    <apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0}" rendered="{!Lead.Scenario2_Primary__c == true}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.Scenario2_Retirement_Age__c}" /></apex:outputText>
                                    <apex:outputText value="{0, number, #0}" rendered="{!AND(Lead.Scenario1_Primary__c == false, Lead.Scenario2_Primary__c == false)}"><apex:param value="{!Lead.Expected_Retirement_Age__c}" /></apex:outputText>
                                </span>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Spouse Social Security:</td>
                            <td class="sign">+</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.Spouse_Social_Security__c}" /></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Military Retirement:</td>
                            <td class="sign">+</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.Military_Retirement__c}" /></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Disability Retirement:</td>
                            <td class="sign">+</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.Disability_in_Retirement__c}" /></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Additional Income:</td>
                            <td class="sign">+</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.Additional_Income1__c}" /></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Additional Income:</td>
                            <td class="sign">+</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.Additional_Income2__c}" /></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="tot">
                            <td class="lab">Total:</td>
                            <td class="sign">=</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!snapIncomeTotal}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">Current Net:</td>
                            <td class="sign">-</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.currentNET__c}" /></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="tot">
                            <td class="lab">Difference:</td>
                            <td class="sign">=</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!snapDifference}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="lab">TSP:</td>
                            <td class="sign">+</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!snapTspDisplay}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                            <td class="extra">Annual Withdrawal &#8212; Traditional: <span class="u"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.AnnualWithdraw1__c}" /></span>&#160; Roth: <span class="u"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.AnnualWithdraw2__c}" /></span>&#160; Tax Rate: <span class="u"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.taxRate5_Picklist__c}" /></span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="tot">
                            <td class="lab">Bottom Line:</td>
                            <td class="sign">=</td>
                            <td class="uval"><apex:outputText value="{0, number, $#,##0.00}"><apex:param value="{!snapBottomLine}" /></apex:outputText></td>
                            <td class="extra">&#160;</td>
                        </tr>
                    </table>

                    <p class="gfgp-center gfgp-italic" style="font-size:9pt;margin-top:14pt;">The information &amp; values shown are for illustration purposes only. These values are not guaranteed as shown.</p>
                </td>
                <td class="gfgp-rail" valign="bottom"><div class="gfgp-pageno">12</div></td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <!-- ============ Pages 13 &amp; 14: Notes ============ -->
        <table class="gfgp-sheet">
            <tr>
                <td class="gfgp-rail" valign="bottom"><div class="gfgp-pageno">13</div></td>
                <td class="gfgp-body">
                    <div class="gfgp-title">Notes</div>
                    <div class="gfgp-accent"></div>
                    <div style="border:1px solid #d0d0d0;min-height:560pt;padding:8pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:11pt;"><apex:outputField value="{!Lead.Description}" /></div>
                </td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <!-- ============ Page 15: Back cover ============ -->
        <div class="gfgp-cover" style="page-break-after:auto;">
            <apex:image url="{!$Resource.Pg16GrovesFedForm}"
                alt="Groves Financial Group" />
        </div>

    </body>
    </html>
</apex:page>
